# As soon as and until in Russian: как только, пока не
subtitle: "Russian time clauses on New Year's Eve: пока́ бьют ку́ранты, как то́лько, пока́ … не, пе́ред тем как, по́сле того́ как, с тех пор как."
tags: ["russian","как только","пока не","time clauses","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/time-clauses","vocabulary/holidays"]
thumb: "band \"Wish while the clock strikes\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Running and swimming in Russian: бегу or бегаю?","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/144-russian-run-swim.cast"}

